c11 (c11 terminal multiplexer)
==============================

c11 is a modified work derived from cmux.

Original work
-------------
Name:     cmux
Author:   manaflow-ai
Source:   https://github.com/manaflow-ai/cmux
License:  GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later (AGPL-3.0-or-later)

Modifications
-------------
Modified by: Stage 11 Agentics
Copyright:   Stage 11 Agentics
Fork point:  cmux main as merged into this repo on 2026-03-18 (57a176bd),
             while cmux was AGPL-3.0-or-later only
Fork date:   2026-04-16 (Stage 11 fork scaffolding, b86b46a7)

Summary of modifications:
- Rebranded app identity (display name "c11", bundle ID "com.stage11.c11").
- New Homebrew tap (stage-11-agentics/c11) and release artifacts
  (c11-macos.dmg) published from the Stage 11 fork.
- Sparkle auto-update feed retargeted to Stage 11 releases.
- Renamed the primary CLI binary from `cmux` to `c11`; the `cmux`
  command remains as a compat alias (in-bundle symlink plus Homebrew
  binary alias). Environment variables `CMUX_*` are still honored
  alongside the new `C11_*` variants (dual-read).
- Socket protocol, shell integration files, and source/module names
  remain identical to upstream cmux for backward compatibility.
- Diverged development after the fork point.

c11 2.0 (developed by Stage 11 as "c11h", a separate app, from
2026-10-31 until it took c11's name on 2026-11-13) adds:
- A bundled, unmodified build of herdr-core (hc), an Apache-2.0
  terminal runtime, as a helper inside the app
  (Contents/Helpers/herdr-core). hc holds every terminal, so terminals
  keep running when the app quits, crashes or updates. Its license and
  pinned commit are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md and
  Resources/hc/hc-source.json.
- Terminal sessions spread across several hc sessions (shards).
- Machine links: terminals on other machines reached over SSH, each
  served by its own hc, shown in the same window.
- A relay through hc that lets agents on a linked machine report
  status, raise flags and exchange mail with the app, and a relay CLI
  kit installed on the linked machine.
- A display-only viewer (`c11 show`) and further CLI verbs (`hc`,
  `machine`, `restore`, `window`, `display`, `chaos`).
- The same release identity as c11 1.x (display name "c11", bundle ID
  "com.stage11.c11", the same Sparkle feed); the earlier "c11h" names
  remain only as compatibility aliases.

Code taken from cmux after the fork point
-----------------------------------------
cmux relicensed to GPL-3.0-or-later on 2026-03-30. Code picked from
cmux after that date (c11 commits 89ec44b8 and b218dcda, 2026-04-27)
is GPL-3.0-or-later and is combined with c11 under section 13 of
GPLv3 and of AGPLv3.

A complete, ongoing record of modifications is available in the git
history of the Stage 11 fork.

